# ================= CONFIGURATION =================
# From https://my.telegram.org  →  API development tools
# This is a ONE-TIME setup step done by whoever deploys the app — it is
# never shown to or entered by whoever logs in from the browser (they only
# ever see phone number → OTP → 2FA password). The same API_ID/API_HASH
# pair can be reused across as many different Telegram phone numbers as
# you like; each login just needs its own separate deployment of this app.
API_ID=
API_HASH=

# ---- Optional overrides ----
# Optional password to lock the dashboard/API/WebSocket. Leave empty = open
# (fine on a trusted LAN). Strongly recommended if you expose this publicly.
# DASHBOARD_PASSWORD=
# Persistent data dir (set to /data on Fly.io with a mounted volume).
# DATA_DIR=/data
# Root that "local path" scanning is confined to (Android/Termux default shown).
# SCAN_ROOT=~/storage/shared/DCIM
# MAX_CONCURRENT_UPLOADS=3
# Files larger than this (bytes) are split into parts. Default ~1.9GB stays
# under Telegram's 2GB free cap; raise toward 4GB on a Premium account. Set
# small (e.g. 5242880 = 5MB) to test chunking.
# CHUNK_SIZE=1992294400
